You are a competitive intelligence analyst. Classify one news article.
Company: {{1.`0`}}
Sector: {{1.`3`}}
Headline: {{2.title}}
Description: {{substring(2.description; 0; 800)}}

Pick EXACTLY ONE category from this list, using the label text verbatim:
Product Launch, Partnership, Funding, Leadership Change, Research Publication, Hiring Signal, Regulatory/Legal, Other

Extract any monetary amount central to the story in suffix notation (e.g. $30B, $500M, $2.5M), or N/A if there is none.

Write a factual 1-2 sentence summary.

Return ONLY raw JSON in exactly this shape, no markdown fences:
{"category": "<one category>", "funding": "<amount or N/A>", "summary": "<1-2 sentence summary>"}

Output ONLY the requested content. Begin directly with the first line of output. Do not include any introductory text, preamble, or closing remarks.

You are writing a daily AI competitive intelligence briefing. Below are today's signals as JSON. Synthesize them into a briefing of at most 5 short paragraphs. Group related items, be factual and specific, and lead with the most significant development.

Signals:{{23.array}}

Output ONLY the briefing text. Begin directly with the first paragraph. No preamble, no closing remarks.
